abstract: >-
  A reception apparatus for the Spiritual Exercises of Ignatius of Loyola in
  the twentieth century, continuing the author's Ignatiana edition. The text
  stands at the centre on the paragraph grid [1]-[370] (Autograph and Vulgate
  after the Monumenta Ignatiana 1919, Mullan 1914, Rickaby 1923, Feder 1922);
  the century's readings stand in the margin as 757 glosses from 32 works and
  104 journal articles in six languages, each with the basis of its placement
  and its access tier. Public-domain texts are quoted and linked to their
  scans; protected works are represented by anchors and summaries only. With
  eight reading paths, an introductory essay, a timeline, a concept atlas, a
  bibliography with BibTeX and RIS export, and public-domain plates.
